-	/** gdm_stag_en: bit0 makes the GDM parse the MediaTek special tag on frames from the switch (vendor GDMA1_VLAN_CHECK, written by macEN7512STagEnable; TPID 0x8100 in bits 31:16 after reset). Then it reports IPv4/IPv6 and drops bad TCP/UDP checksums, but on GS2107 every frame then took about 7 ms round trip (0.5 ms without), TCP fell to a few Mb/s and every received frame carried a CPU reason (last one decoded crsn=30, ppe_entry=1), which suggests a detour through the FE/PPE path that the vendor sets up with hw_nat.ko (not verified). The driver leaves it off. */
+	/** gdm_stag_en: bit0 makes the GDM parse the MediaTek special tag of frames from the switch (vendor GDMA1_VLAN_CHECK, which macEN7512STagEnable writes as the whole word 1; TPID 0x8100 in bits 31:16 after reset). The PPE only builds entries for frames behind the tag with it set; the GDM then also reports IPv4/IPv6 and drops bad TCP/UDP checksums, and frames that come through the PPE carry source ports other than GDM1 (9, 11, 12 seen) in the RX descriptor. Set together with the DMA tag parsing when the PPE is used (en75_set_dsa_tag_parse()). */
